y": "{\"answer\": \"According to the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001, p. 77), for the Rosemount 3051CFC Compact Orifice Flow Meter with Conditioning Option C in Ranges 2–3, a beta ratio (β) of 0.50 gives a flow reference accuracy of ±1.95% of flow rate at 8:1 flow turndown. This applies to the FT-21-3 flow measurement loop shown on the P&ID.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "c01", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The transmitter feeding FIC-12-1 is FT-12-1, which is covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (00813-0100-4001). On transmitter failure the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; the default is a high alarm (≥21.75 mA, or ≥22.5 mA for the NAMUR-compliant configuration), while a low alarm is ≤3.75 mA (≤3.6 mA NAMUR). The high or low failure mode is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. The alarm direction/levels can also be set at ordering time via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), CR/CS (custom high/low alarm and saturation levels, requiring option C1), or CT (Rosemount standard low alarm); these alarm-level options are only available with the HART 4–20 mA output (code A).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [88, 15, 109, 46, 35, 86, 83, 74, 57, 26, 42, 62]}], "latency_s": 2.027846699988004, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 193818, "completion_tokens": 416, "cost_usd": 0.00672704, "spent_usd": 0.00672667, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 88, "score": 0.5907}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 15, "score": 0.5372}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 109, "score": 0.535}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 46, "score": 0.5277}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 35, "score": 0.5274}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 86, "score": 0.5254}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 83, "score": 0.5212}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 74, "score": 0.5107}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 57, "score": 0.5079}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 26, "score": 0.5075}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 42, "score": 0.5047}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 62, "score": 0.5041}], "prompt_chars": 481220, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The transmitter feeding FIC-12-1 is FT-12-1, which is covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (00813-0100-4001). On transmitter failure the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; the default is a high alarm (≥21.75 mA, or ≥22.5 mA for the NAMUR-compliant configuration), while a low alarm is ≤3.75 mA (≤3.6 mA NAMUR). The high or low failure mode is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. The alarm direction/levels can also be set at ordering time via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), CR/CS (custom high/low alarm and saturation levels, requiring option C1), or CT (Rosemount standard low alarm); these alarm-level options are only available with the HART 4–20 mA output (code A).\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "c02", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The item directly downstream of BV-14-1 is GV-14-2 (the PG-57 line from BV-14-1 continues onto sheet 4 into GV-14-2), which is covered by the GFPS Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet. According to that datasheet's spare parts section, you can buy parts on their own: a coil set (available separately for 24V DC, 230V AC and 110V AC, in EPDM or FKM versions) and a wear part set (available in several size ranges, EPDM or FKM). A seal kit is not offered for this valve in the documents; seal kits appear only in the Swagelok check valve datasheet, which does not apply to GV-14-2. So you do not have to replace the whole unit - the coil (and wear parts) can be ordered separately.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "pages": [6, 4]}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36, 16, 8, 7, 6]}, {"document_id": "swagelok-ms-01-176", "pages": [15]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [96, 93, 36, 11]}], "latency_s": 5.3913260999834165, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 193518, "completion_tokens": 650, "cost_usd": 0.00679834, "spent_usd": 0.00679834, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 6, "score": 0.5492}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.549}, {"document_id": "swagelok-ms-01-176", "page": 15, "score": 0.5118}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 16, "score": 0.5085}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 8, "score": 0.5039}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 7, "score": 0.501}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 6, "score": 0.4992}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page"